<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Apr-Nov exchequer receipts 95 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African Apr-Nov exchequer receipts 95 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total exchequer receipts in the first eight months of the 1996/97 (April-March) financial year were 95.065 billion rand, or about 65.6 percent of the total budget of 144.9 billion rand, the Finance Department said.</p>
<p>Exchequer receipts in November 1996 were 10.139 billion rand, 18.6 percent more than in November last year.</p>
<p>During November 1996 financing of 3.367 billion rand was obtained in government bonds while short term loans (net) increased by 1.707 billion rand, bringing the total financing for November 1996 to 5.075 billion rand.</p>
<p>The following are key Apr-Nov figures:</p>
<p>(rand bln)		Nov '96  Oct '96  Apr/Nov'96   Apr/Nov'95</p>
<p>Exchequer issues	14.647   13.634  113.751	   99.371</p>
<p>Total revenue	   10.139   15.697   95.065	   81.076</p>
<p>Borrowing requirement  0.429   (4.267)  28.231	   24.311</p>
<p>Total financing	  5.075    5.724   32.876	   32.057</p>
<p>Main sources of revenue:</p>
<p>				Oct '96   Sep'96  Apr/Oct'96  Apr/Oct'95</p>
<p>    Income tax	    8.832     8.499   45.914	37.890</p>
<p>Sales tax/VAT	 2.862     3.448   20.127	18.395</p>
<p>Customs and Excise  1.439     1.939   11.014	 9.525</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
